cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Home Front in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Home Front"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Home Front is an open-source, self-hosted productivity app and daily journal that shows
  your life as a 1936 grand-strategy war map. You say what happened today in a sentence;
  it files a dated entry, judges it with the AI provider you choose (or an offline judge),
  and the front for that part of your life advances or gives ground.
authors:
  - name: "Home Front contributors"
version: "1.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sam-siavoshian/homefront-map"
url: "https://homefront-map.vercel.app/"
keywords:
  - self-hosted
  - productivity
  - journal
  - habit tracker
  - life tracker
  - quantified self
  - local-first
  - grand strategy
